Round-3 codex gpt-5.6-sol relaunch on ls20 (after the first attempt burned
~19 of 40 minutes on an unrelated REPL stall and timed out with no
artifact). Found a 62-action route consuming all three counter rings and
the C->9->E->8 pinwheel, but both tested lower-pad orientations were
rejected -- confirming round 2's exact prediction that a separate upper
black-dot tile must select the target SHAPE before the lower-pad
ORIENTATION sequence; this candidate omitted the shape-selection step
entirely. Fresh reproduce() gate on the full 308-action candidate
deterministically reached level 4, not 5.

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 4.
Next attempt should insert an upper black-dot visit before the lower-pad
sequence.

